Fedora-only fix-up, kept here on purpose (the patch series must also apply to vanilla stable): kernel-ark's
kernel-7.2.10-0 carries five more entries in ipu-bridge's upside_down_sensor_dmi_ids table than vanilla
v7.2.10, so the context of the 7.2 rotation-quirk patch (Surface Pro 8 and 9) doesn't match there and
`git am -3` can't fall back to a merge. This changes only that hunk's context to kernel-ark's, as
orthogonaleety/linux-surface's f44-7.2.10-0 branch does; the lines added are the same.
(`git apply` warns about "space before tab": that's a context line of the inner patch, and it
must stay as it is.)
---
